family: line-cli
what: poll
transport: v2c
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: common line-oriented SNMP commands (snmp-server community, snmp-server group, snmp-server user); RFC 3414 and RFC 3415
does: Lets Woodshed poll the device's SNMP agent (SNMPv2c, read-only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with the device's name and interfaces; after the first cycle the device page shows its graphs.
placeholders: <COMMUNITY>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Limit the agent to polls from Woodshed's address (192.0.2.10): most devices take an access list or a host list on the community or group line, written differently on each.
- Some devices also need the agent turned on (`snmp-server enable`, or a per-interface management setting) before they answer.
- Then add the device in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, SNMPv2c and the same community.
---- part cli "": Enter in global configuration mode, fill in the placeholders, then save the configuration
snmp-server community <COMMUNITY> ro
==== text
! Enter in global configuration mode, fill in the placeholders, then save the configuration
